1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,900
Is a house
made of brick,

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:04,368
or bricks? Both
are correct.

3
00:00:04,903 --> 00:00:06,034
Think of gold.

4
00:00:06,074 --> 00:00:07,917
A ring, a coin
and a necklace

5
00:00:07,957 --> 00:00:09,337
are three things.

6
00:00:09,377 --> 00:00:10,667
Gold
is the substance they

7
00:00:10,707 --> 00:00:11,772
are made from.

8
00:00:11,812 --> 00:00:14,037
So we ask:
how much gold?

9
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:16,117
I count three rings,

10
00:00:16,157 --> 00:00:18,461
or measure twenty
grams of gold.

11
00:00:18,501 --> 00:00:20,913
The number goes
on rings or grams,

12
00:00:20,953 --> 00:00:22,216
not on gold.

13
00:00:23,137 --> 00:00:24,387
Now the house.

14
00:00:24,427 --> 00:00:26,123
‘Made of bricks’
means individual

15
00:00:26,163 --> 00:00:27,786
blocks you
could count.

16
00:00:27,826 --> 00:00:30,016
‘Made of brick’
names the material.

17
00:00:30,056 --> 00:00:31,307
Both are right.

18
00:00:31,347 --> 00:00:32,892
The difference
is what the word

19
00:00:32,932 --> 00:00:34,911
names in your
sentence.

